# Every text file is stored in the repository with LF, whatever a contributor's
# platform checks it out with. That held when this rule was written and stopped
# holding immediately: Dependabot #319 committed mvnw.cmd and mvnwDebug.cmd with
# CRLF blobs, because a commit made through the GitHub API never runs the clean
# filter this file configures. 4.4.1 renormalised them. The rule cannot enforce
# itself, so build.yml re-checks it on every PR.
* text=auto

# The Maven wrapper's Windows scripts ship from upstream with CRLF, while the copies
# here are LF. Without a rule, every wrapper bump rewrites all of mvnw.cmd and
# mvnwDebug.cmd line by line: Dependabot #319 carried 216 changed lines across the two
# for a change that touched neither. Storing them as LF and checking them out as CRLF
# keeps that diff to the lines that actually moved, and Windows still gets the line
# endings cmd.exe expects.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# mvnw is a POSIX shell script and must keep LF even on a Windows checkout, or the
# shell rejects it. Git Bash and WSL both run this file.
mvnw text eol=lf

# Windows-1252 and UTF-16 have no business here, and a .jar or image must never be
# line-ending filtered.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.jfr binary
